FINAL ANSWER:
The library code (`lib/index.js`) depends on one person: **Troy Goode**. They hold 67.3% of its surviving lines. The test suite also depends on them at the folder level (51.2%), and Douglas Christopher Wilson holds most of the rest. The whole project has a bus factor of **2**.

I used the `surviving-lines` tool. It runs `git blame -w -M -C` at HEAD and counts the lines each author still has in the code, which is a better ownership signal than commit counts. It covered all 18 files: 1,662 non-blank lines (1,995 with blank lines), 315 commits, merges excluded.

## Whole repository

**Bus factor = 2.** I define bus factor as the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50% of the code. Counting the two Troy Goode addresses as one person, Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson hold 72.2% of non-blank lines (72.5% with blank lines). It takes 4 authors to reach 80%.

| Author | Lines | Share | With blank | Share | Commits | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 649 | 39.0% | 810 | 40.8% | 95 (30.2%) | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 | 33.2% | 629 | 31.7% | 143 (45.4%) | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 80 | 4.8% | 95 | 4.8% | 2 | 2024-05-14 |
| Jon Church | 59 | 3.5% | 72 | 3.6% | 3 | 2026-01-16 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 | 3.4% | 67 | 3.4% | 2 | 2025-07-23 |
| Ulises Gascón | 46 | 2.8% | 52 | 2.6% | 3 | 2026-01-22 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 38 | 2.3% | 44 | 2.2% | 2 | 2025-12-01 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 | 1.8% | 34 | 1.7% | 5 | 2015-05-28 |
| Linus Unnebäck | 26 | 1.6% | 26 | 1.3% | 1 | 2016-11-07 |
| Ollie Buck | 14 | 0.8% | 17 | 0.9% | 1 | 2019-06-05 |

52 more authors hold 6.7% together; the largest is Eric di Domenico with 0.7%.

**Troy Goode appears under two addresses.** I counted `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example` as one person because the name is identical and the tool rates the match as strong. That is still a guess from names and addresses. Counted separately, the two addresses hold 605 lines (36.4%) and 44 lines (2.6%); the bus factor is still 2 (69.6%), and it takes 5 authors to reach 80%. The `.mailmap` line that would make the merge permanent comes from `--identities`. I did not run that or write anything.

## Parts that depend on one person

| Scope | Bus factor (50%) | Main holder |
|---|---|---|
| `lib/` (only `lib/index.js`, 214 lines) | **1** | Troy Goode 67.3%; next is Douglas Christopher Wilson at 9.3% |
| `test/` (820 lines) | **1** | Troy Goode 51.2%; Douglas Christopher Wilson 42.0% |
| root files (323 lines) | 2 | Douglas Christopher Wilson 29.4%, Troy Goode 26.3% |
| `.github/` (305 lines) | 2 | Douglas Christopher Wilson 30.2%, Íñigo Marquínez Prado 26.2% |

Single files where one person holds more than 80%:
- **Troy Goode:**
  - `test/vary.js`: 100%
  - `test/error-response.js`: 82.7%
  - `test/example-app.js`: 80.0%
  - `test/issue-2.js`: 80.0%
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson:**
  - `LICENSE`: 94.4%
  - `HISTORY.md`: 80.5%
  - `.eslintrc.yml`, `test/.eslintrc.yml`, `test/support/env.js`: 100%
- **Íñigo Marquínez Prado:** `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml`, 98.4%
- **Sebastian Beltran:** `.github/workflows/codeql.yml`, 100%
- **Ulises Gascón:** `.github/dependabot.yml`, 100%

Overall, 10 of the 18 files have one owner above 80%. Three files have no owner above 50%, so they depend on several people: `test/test.js` (Douglas Christopher Wilson 49.8%, Troy Goode 41.3%), `README.md`, and `package.json`. `package.json` is borderline: Douglas Christopher Wilson holds exactly 50.0%.

**Practical risk:** Douglas Christopher Wilson's last commit was in 2021. That makes Troy Goode the main person who knows the core library, and most of the test suite is also theirs.

## What I excluded or checked

- **Reformat commit left out:** `62628c0` by Fiona Formatter (2026-04-12) only changed indentation and quotes, in 4 files (1,016 lines changed). Counting it would give Fiona Formatter 291 lines (17.5%). It would also cut Troy Goode to 554 (33.3%) and Douglas Christopher Wilson to 376 (22.6%), and the top two together would drop to 56.0%.
- **Other mechanical-looking commits:** the tool checked 136 commits and set aside only `62628c0`. It kept 5 others that look mechanical: `739dc11`, `fcd2b56`, `00d6eec`, `344ce1e` and `9c2b59d`. Each holds 17 lines or fewer, so they do not change these results.
- **Bot:** dependabot[bot] (10 lines, 11 commits) is not credited.
- **Same address, two names:** "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" and "alex94puchades" use the same address and are counted as one person (30 lines).
- **Lines not attributed:** 10 of the 1,672 non-blank lines were not credited to anyone (1,662 attributed).

These numbers measure whose code is still in the project. They do not show code quality, review work, or who actually understands the code.

